      "facts": [
        "Kitty-protocol keyboards encode plain Enter as an escape sequence (e.g. \\x1b[13u) but report modifiers reliably, so the escape-prefix and raw \\r/\\n heuristics (which exist to catch legacy Alt+Enter) must not apply to kitty events."
      ],
      "title": "CLI update: multiline-input",
      "summary": "CLI changes across 1 file(s) (+115/−64).",
      "tags": [
        "cli"
      ],
      "day": "2026-06-10",
      "month": "2026-06",
      "category": "CLI",
      "significance": "minor",
      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix plain Enter detection for Kitty protocol keyboards",
        "summary": "MultilineInput now treats key.source === 'kitty' as a valid Enter signal, bypassing legacy escape-prefix and raw \\r/\\n heuristics. This prevents plain Enter from being misinterpreted as Alt+Enter on Kitty-protocol terminals, which encode Enter as an escape sequence (e.g. \\x1b[13u) while reliably reporting modifiers. Change scoped to cli/src/components/multiline-input.tsx. The isKittyKey flag explicitly disables hasEscapePrefix checks for these events to ensure accurate modifier state.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:22:30.502Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you press Enter in the CLI's new interactive input on a Kitty-protocol terminal, it now reliably inserts a new line instead of being mistaken for Alt+Enter, which had been adding unwanted paragraph breaks. The terminal sends Enter as a special encoded sequence, and the input handler now recognizes that encoding format directly rather than running it through legacy Alt+Enter detection, so plain Enter, Shift+Enter, and Alt+Enter each behave as expected on these keyboards.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "484bbe95c8e9",
